---
/* Split — the trip's budgeting and bill-splitting tool (design-system.md §11, §27). One ledger
   per guide, on the guide's own storeKey; the destination is a thin frame around the calculator
   so the engine, its validation, currency handling, payments and undo stay exactly where they
   are (features/trip-split). Recent Expenses + Add Expense lead; balances follow. On desktop a
   destination-derived scene (the same Painted Atlas the covers use) stands dimmed behind the
   opaque working surface — scenery never outranks the numbers.

   Surface 8 (board `08_split_expenses`, Sonnet 5): Split is now one of the frame strip's own
   tabs (design-system.md §6 phone-bar list), not a page reached by a back-button — the old
   "← Trip" header this destination drew for itself is retired in favour of the frame's own
   navigation, and .split-title/.split-desc (already the calculator's own heading) become the
   visible header. .spatial turns the whole panel forest in both themes, matching the frame
   pattern every other surface already shares (§1). */
import TripSplit from "./TripSplit.astro";
import PaintedAtlas from "./PaintedAtlas.astro";
interface Props { storeKey: string; slug?: string; tz?: string | null }
const { storeKey, slug = storeKey, tz = null } = Astro.props;
---
<div class="splitdest spatial">
  <div class="splitdest-scene" aria-hidden="true"><PaintedAtlas seed={slug} tz={tz ?? undefined} mini={true} /></div>
  <TripSplit storeKey={storeKey} standalone />
</div>
